1,Recordings of Xârâgurè: An Austronesian language of Southern New ...,https://www.elararchive.org/dk0589/,"In addition, Xârâgurè is also spoken on the west coast, in Ouinané, where the Xârâgurè community used to live before being chased by the French colonization. Language information Xârâgurè is an Austronesian language, belonging to the Southern New Caledonian subgroup (Austronesian > Oceanic > New Caledonian > Southern).",Xârâgurè,Austronesian
2,Austronesian Music - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/@austronesianmusic6149,"Hi everyone! Welcome to Austronesian Music🎶This channel mainly posts music from Austronesian countries and languages, and also other songs of languages of Southeast Asia. Hope you all enjoy🤗 ...",Xârâgurè,Austronesian
3,"Recordings in Xârâcùù and Xârâgurè (Thio, New Caledonia)",https://researchdata.edu.au/recordings-xrc-xrgur-new-caledonia/,"Recordings in Xârâcùù and Xârâgurè (Thio, New Caledonia) made in 1977, 1980 and 1984. Data includes stories, conversation, history stories, names, song and chants.",Xârâgurè,Austronesian
4,Pangloss Collection | Xârâgurè corpus,https://pangloss.cnrs.fr/corpus/Xârâgurè?mode=pro&lang=en,"Xârâgurè is one of the 28 Kanak languages, of the Austronesian language family, spoken in the Xaracùù customary area of the South Province, New Caledonia. This language is spoken by about 700 speakers.",Xârâgurè,Austronesian
5,Austronesian Music - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLnOSH5j1sQh9pFS_rqvm3r2JtCD8AGOa-,"Austronesian culture includes more than 1200 ethnic groups, across South Asia, Southeast Asia, Taiwan, the Philippines, parts of China, as well as the Pacific as far afield as the Maori in New ...",Xârâgurè,Austronesian
6,Xârâgurè - Sorosoro,https://www.sorosoro.org/en/xaragure/,"Some speakers of Xârâgurè also live in Ouinané, on the West coast of the main island (la Grande Terre). Classification: Like all Kanak languages (with the exception of Fagauvea), Xârâgurè belongs to the Oceanic branch of the Austronesian Language family.",Xârâgurè,Austronesian
7,Austronesian Music - Music genre - Rate Your Music,https://rateyourmusic.com/genre/austronesian-music/,"Austronesian music nowadays refers to the ongoing evolution and fusion of various cultural influences from foreign and neighbouring cultures. These influences have over the centuries introduced new instruments, styles, and genres, blending age-old elements with newer traditions.",Xârâgurè,Austronesian
8,OLAC resources in and about the Xârâgurè language,http://language-archives.org/language/axx,"ISO 639-3: axx The combined catalog of all OLAC participants contains the following resources that are relevant to this language: Primary texts Language descriptions Other resources about the language Other resources in the language Other known names and dialect names: 'Aragure, Aragure, Borendy, Borindi, Haragure, Naa Xaragure, Thio",Xârâgurè,Austronesian
9,ABVD: Xârâgurè,https://abvd.eva.mpg.de/austronesian/language.php?id=1609,"Seen an error? Please let us know: hand left right leg/foot to walk road/path to come to turn to swim dirty dust skin back belly bone intestines liver breast shoulder to know, be knowledgeable to think to fear blood head neck hair nose to breathe to sniff, smell mouth tooth tongue to laugh to cry to vomit to spit to eat to chew to cook to drink to bite to suck ear to hear eye to see to yawn to ...",Xârâgurè,Austronesian
